  "text": "Recipe: Moong & Quinoa Cheela\nCreator: Kusum Dhairyawan\nCategory: Cheela\nIngredients: green split moong daal, quinoa, ginger, green chillies, curry leaves, spinach, cilantro, green onions, hing (asafoetida), cumin seeds, fennel seeds, black pepper powder, black sesame seeds, grated carrots, Cilantro & Mint Chutney\nCooking methods: no-cook, blend, saute\nInstructions: SOAKING: Soak 1 cup green split moong daal and 1/2 cup quinoa overnight, or at least for 4-5 hours.\nBATTER: After soaking, grind them with 1 inch piece of ginger, 1-2 green chillies, a few curry leaves and a handful of spinach. Grind to a smooth consistency. Add the following to the batter & mix well:\n*   Chopped cilantro\n*   Chopped green onions (2 stalks)\n*   Spices: hing (asafoetida), cumin seeds, fennel seeds, black pepper powder\nCHEELA: Pour batter onto a griddle and cook both sides to make Cheelas.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (quinoa), BEANS (green split moong dal), LEAFY GREENS (spinach), RAINBOW VEGGIES (green onion), NUTS & SEEDS (black sesame seeds), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
